  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 103 PM MDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nThursday evening starts off this long term period with \nmonsoonal moisture moving in, and a shortwave moving through the\narea. With precipitable water values in the 1-1.5 range, RH \nvalues 60-90%, and the shortwave, its safe to say our area will \nbe getting some much needed moisture. This moisture sticks \naround through Monday, bringing daily afternoon chances of \nprecipitation. This precipitation looks to mainly be showers, \nbut an isolated thunderstorm cannot be ruled out especially near\nthe NE panhandle with CAPE values near 1000J/kg. Winds do not \nappear to be out of the ordinary, staying below 15 knots most of\nthe time. Temperatures cool off as a cold front moves over the \narea Thursday. 700mb temperatures stay near 12C during the \ndaytime Thursday-Sunday, with nighttime temperatures getting \nnear 10C. This means temperatures will cool off nearly 20F from \nwhat we have been experiencing. Typically our area has daytime \ntemperatures near 83F this time of year. This is a welcomed \nbreak from our hot temperatures the last few weeks. With all of \nthis monsoonal moisture coming in, fire weather is not a concern\nthrough this long term period.",
